;; differences (test/haskell/roundtrip-ghc-9.14.1-text-known.edn: the module printed back byte for byte, byte-identical in every
;; case; the difference is GHC's trees of mode :full), in goi's format. A module is in the first class whose :match finds its
;; "RESULT REASON". Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :module-view-comments
  :title "a header's comments outside the module view"
  :kind :design
  :why "the three modules that #include \"CTypes.h\", a header with Haskell comments: the original's tree in mode :full holds the header's comments (spans in include/CTypes.h), which the module view (SPEC 2.8, S5) leaves out with the header's other lines, so GHC attaches the module's own documentation otherwise; the printed text is byte-identical"
  :decided "R3; SPEC 2.8, S5"
  :match [#"include/CTypes.h's comments"]}
 {:id :module-view-include
  :title "a CPP #include of Haskell source"
  :kind :design
  :why "the module's text is another file's (a CPP #include of Haskell source: bytestring's ReadInt and ReadNat, filepath's and os-string's Posix and Windows modules): outside the module view, whose conversion in mode :full names the other file's lines; the printed text is byte-identical"
  :decided "R5; SPEC 2.8, S5; HR18"
  :match [#"another file's, a CPP #include of Haskell source"]}
]
